gram and is not attached to this release; its manifest and public inputs are kept for comparison.\nL174: The documentation reports the v1.2.0 measurements against v1.1.0 measured on the same days and instance types: on one 192-core VM, a p99 latency of 34 ms at 1,000 requests/s against 440 ms, and 3,300 requests/s with every request accepted within one second against 1,150/s.\nL175: StateSync-GKR v1.1.1 and later versions are licensed under the Business Source License 1.1. Research and other non-production use are free, and production use solely to verify proofs is granted. Production proving, and redistribution or services that provide proving functionality, require the commercial license described in LICENSE. Versions up to and including v1.1.0 were released under MIT OR Apache-2.0. Contribution and dependency notices are recorded in NOTICE and the software bill of materials.\nL176: Software DOI: 【65†10.5281/zenodo.23655511†doi.org】. Release notes: 【66†release/v1.2/RELEASE_NOTES.md】.\nL177: \nL178: Download the 17 assets and follow REPRODUCING.md to verify them. SHA256SUMS lists the attachment digests, and the source archive is built deterministically.\nL179: \nL180: Assets 20\nL181: \nL182:   * 【67†statesync-gkr-v1.1-proof-manifest.json】\nL183: \nL184: sha256:880456ed769f8c1bc41883b15b418300c28b01b1f2aec54c09f2a38fe25761df\nL185: \nL186: 3.79 KB 2026-10-26T08:48:09Z\nL187: \nL188:   * 【68†statesync-gkr-v1.1-public-inputs.json】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCommits · quangvdao/monomial-sumcheck-benchmarks · GitHub (https://github.com/quangvdao/monomial-sumcheck-benchmarks/commits/main/)\nciteturn3view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/quangvdao/monomial-sumcheck-benchmarks/commits/main/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 456\nL0: 【0†Skip to content】\nL1: ## Navigation Menu\nL2: \nL3: 【1†Sign in】\nL4: \nL5: Appearance settings\nL6: \nL7: 